### What is a generalized abbreviation?

A generalized abbreviation of a word is any string where one or more contiguous groups of characters have been replaced by the count of characters in that group. For the word `loan`, some valid abbreviations are:

- `loan` (keep all four characters)
- `l3` (keep `l`, abbreviate `oan` as 3)
- `1o2` (abbreviate `l` as 1, keep `o`, abbreviate `an` as 2)
- `4` (abbreviate the entire word as 4)

The problem asks you to generate all such abbreviations. For a word of length n, there are exactly 2^n abbreviations because each character is independently either kept or counted.

```java
package com.bank.coding;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * Generates all unique generalized abbreviations of a word.
 */
public class GeneralizedAbbreviations {

    public static List<String> generateAbbreviations(String word) {
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        backtrack(word, 0, new StringBuilder(), 0, result);
        return result;
    }

    private static void backtrack(String word, int index,
                                   StringBuilder current, int count,
                                   List<String> result) {
        int savedLength = current.length();

        if (index == word.length()) {
            if (count > 0) current.append(count);
            result.add(current.toString());
            current.setLength(savedLength); // backtrack
            return;
        }

        // Branch 1: abbreviate this character (increment count)
        backtrack(word, index + 1, current, count + 1, result);

        // Branch 2: keep this character as a literal
        if (count > 0) current.append(count);
        current.append(word.charAt(index));
        backtrack(word, index + 1, current, 0, result);
        current.setLength(savedLength); // backtrack
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> abbreviations = generateAbbreviations("loan");
        System.out.println("Total: " + abbreviations.size());
        abbreviations.forEach(System.out::println);
    }
}
```

